        "original_id": "4cf7a073-d37d-52af-ba3d-354896a8951f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ghostkeeper, Lonesome Dove: The Series\n- People: Jim Makichuk, Georgie Collins\n- Concepts: Windigo legend, Wendigo psychosis\n- Topics: Canadian independent horror films, culture-bound syndromes\n\nFacts:\n- Ghostkeeper is a 1981 Canadian independent horror film directed by Jim Makichuk.\n- Ghostkeeper has a plot inspired by the Windigo legend of North America.\n- Georgie Collins is known for her role in the 1981 cult horror film Ghostkeeper.\n- Georgie Collins also appeared in Lonesome Dove: The Series in 1995.\n- The Windigo or Wendigo legend gave its name to the modern medical term Wendigo psychosis.\n- Psychiatrists have described Wendigo psychosis as a controversial culture-bound syndrome involving an intense craving for human flesh and a fear of becoming a cannibal.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
